` THE NEW KINDS OF FISH. three cards each put a new kind of thing on the board. each one is a kind of
` fish like any other: it has a picture, it can be swapped, and three of it in a row pop. load_textures,
` in fish_routines, loads the pictures right after the first seven fish, so that they are fish 8, 9 and 10.
global TEX_JELLY
global TEX_RAY
global TEX_BOTTLE

` JELLIES. with the "jellies" card, some of the new fish that drop in are jellyfish. when a jellyfish
` pops, every fish right next to it has a chance of its own to get stung, and a fish that is stung
` goes belly up. a belly up fish pops when the cursor comes to it, the same as with "bottoms up".
` getRandomValue and stingJelly, in fish_funcs, do it.
global JELLY_SPAWN_CHANCE = 10 `how many new fish in a hundred are jellyfish
global JELLY_STING_CHANCE = 50 `how many fish in a hundred get stung, of the ones next to a jellyfish that pops

` RAYS. with the "rays" card, some of the new fish are stingrays. a stingray that lands on the bottom
` row, from a row above it, shoots up its column, and every fish in the column pops, from the bottom
` to the top, as one group. the stingray goes with them. fishHitBottom, in fish_funcs, is where it starts.
global RAY_SPAWN_CHANCE = 4 `how many new fish in a hundred are stingrays

` BOTTLES. with the "bottles" card, a group of fish that matched, and that is big enough, leaves a
` bottle behind, in the cell of the group that is closest to the middle of it. the bottle falls like a
` fish does, and it can be swapped like one. when it is on the bottom row, it adds to the multiplier,
` and it is gone. handle_combos leaves the bottle, and checkBottles, in fish_funcs, pays it out.
global BOTTLE_GROUP_SIZE = 5 `how many fish a group needs to leave a bottle
global BOTTLE_MULT_GAIN = 1 `how much a bottle adds to the multiplier

` THE WASTE BUCKET. a special move that pops every belly up fish on the board at once, as one group,
` and they score WASTE_BUCKET_BONUS times as much. it never has to recharge, but it does count as a move.
` when there are no belly up fish, it does nothing, and it is not a move. doWasteBucket, in fish_funcs, does it.
global WASTE_BUCKET_BONUS = 2

` BUNCH UP. a special move that is a swap. the fish that the swap connects do not pop. they all go
` into a stack behind the fish that was swapped, and the cells that they leave fill back in. a stack
` made this way can be taller than the cards can make one, up to BUNCH_STACK_MAX, though only the
` first few show. a swap that connects nothing is still a swap. doBunchUp, in fish_funcs, does it.
global BUNCH_STACK_MAX = 9 `the saved game has room for one digit
global BUNCH_UP_COOLDOWN = 2 `this counts the move itself, so there is one move to wait

` FORCED POPS. a cell with a comboForce pops the next time that handle_combos looks at the board, no
` matter what is in it, and the cells that have the same number pop as one group. these are the numbers.
` 1 is a belly up fish that the cursor came to.
global FORCE_BUCKET = 2 `the belly up fish of the waste bucket, which score more
global FORCE_BUNCH = 3 `fish that are going into a stack. they go away without popping, and score nothing.
global FORCE_RAY = 10 `a column that a stingray shot up. the column is added to this.
global FORCE_BOTTLE = 40 `a bottle that paid out. the column is added to this too.

` THE ROBOT. a special move that makes swaps for the player. it looks at the fish near the cursor, picks
` the swap that would pop the most fish, makes it, and then does that again, a few times over.
` the swaps do not count as moves of their own, and they do not touch the multiplier. the whole thing
` counts as the one move. doRobot, in fish_funcs, does it.
global ROBOT_SWAPS = 3 `how many swaps it makes
global ROBOT_REACH = 2 `how many cells away from the cursor it looks, in every direction
global ROBOT_COOLDOWN = 2 `how many moves it takes to recharge
global ROBOT_SWAP_TIME = 170 `how long each of its swaps takes, in milliseconds
global ROBOT_STAMP = 1000000 `a number that is different for every search that it makes. see robotGroupSize.
global ROBOT_LAST_COUNT = 0 `how many swaps it made the last time. 0 means that it found nothing to do.

` THE ERASER. a special move that sorts the whole board, with a flurry of quick swaps, so that every
` kind of fish ends up all together, and then all of it pops.
` it sorts along a path that snakes through the board: left to right along the top row, back from right
` to left along the next one, and so on down. two cells that are next to each other on the path are
` next to each other on the board, so every swap that it makes is one that the player could have made.
` once the path is sorted, each kind of fish is one unbroken stretch of it, and so one group.
` a kind that there are too few of to pop on their own gets popped anyway, so that nothing is left over.
` doEraser, in fish_funcs, does it.
global ERASER_COOLDOWN = 6 `how many moves it takes to recharge
global ERASER_SPEED_START# = 1 `how many swaps it makes on its first frame
global ERASER_SPEED_GROW# = .35 `how many more it makes on every frame after that, so that it starts slow enough to follow and then tears through
global ERASER_SPEED_MAX# = 60 `the most that it makes on a frame

